# <%= title %>

Checks and tasks that take time. Each step's `timeout` is how many
seconds its blocks may run before they are stopped (600 when it is not
set). A `background` block has no timeout: it runs until it is stopped,
while later steps run. A `terminal` block is one the operator runs in
their own shell.

<% if single_file -%>
Everything above the first `##` heading is the preamble. Each `##` heading
below is a step, and its attributes (`kind`, `timeout`, ...) go in the HTML
comment right after the heading.
<% else -%>
Everything above the first step is the preamble. The steps are the files in
`steps/`, run in the order of their numbers, and each one's attributes
(`kind`, `timeout`, ...) are in its front matter.
<% end -%>
